# This repository is PUBLIC and the application handles customer PII and
# payment credentials. These rules are deliberately broad: the cost of an
# over-broad rule is one `git add -f`, the cost of a gap is a disclosure.
#
# Before adding an exception, ask what it would look like on the public
# internet.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- toolchain
node_modules
.next
out
build
dist
.vercel
.turbo
*.tsbuildinfo
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
coverage
.nyc_output
.cache

# ------------------------------------------------------------- environment
# Every .env variant, then the one file that is meant to be committed is
# re-admitted explicitly. `.env.example` must never contain a real value.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Derivatives of an env file. `.env.local.bak` was created by an agent on
# 2026-08-21 and was NOT matched by the previous `.env*.local` rule, which is
# why these are enumerated rather than assumed.
*.bak
*.backup
*.orig
*.rej
*.tmp
*.temp
*.old
*.save
*~
.env*.bak
.env*.backup
.env*.orig
.env*.tmp
.env*.old
.env*.save

